#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:6
msgid ""
"Endpoint configuration belongs to your integration. Vendor updates do not "
"automatically expand your allowlist. Update the exact paths in Scripts, "
"publish, and verify real traffic. These examples are starting points; "
"consult the linked vendor documentation for current requirements."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:9
msgid ""
"Add the external script URL, its consent category/service, and the data-"
"website-id attribute. Enable proxying."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:10
msgid ""
"Allow POST /api/send, or the exact custom collection path configured on your "
"Umami server. Set the runtime host if it differs from the script host."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:11
msgid ""
"The proxy supplies data-host-url unless you override it in Additional "
"attributes. Publish, grant consent, and confirm real POST requests use your "
"local proxy URL."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:15
msgid ""
"Allow GET and POST for the exact collector path, for example /matomo.php or /"
"analytics/matomo.php for a subdirectory installation. In your consent-gated "
"initialization code, point setTrackerUrl at the local proxy base URL "
"followed by that path, and setSiteId to your site ID. Loading matomo.js "
"through the proxy alone does not reroute collection. Keep initialization "
"before the external tracker; remove duplicate theme/plugin installations."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:20
msgid ""
"Use Google’s documented tag gateway or server-side tagging setup for first-"
"party delivery. This generic WordPress proxy is not a replacement for a "
"Google tagging server. If integrating an existing supported collection "
"setup, configure only its verified paths and methods. A proxied gtag.js or "
"GTM container does not automatically reroute its tags, and data-host-url is "
"not a universal Google setting."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:22
msgid "Other services"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:23
msgid ""
"For Meta, LinkedIn, TikTok, Clarity, and Hotjar, use vendor-supported "
"routing and inspect real network requests before configuring paths. No "
"generic complete-proxy recipe is claimed. Keep YouTube, Vimeo, Maps, and "
"CAPTCHA widgets directly loaded behind the appropriate consent gate unless a "
"vendor documents a supported alternative. Do not proxy or cache Turnstile’s "
"script."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:25
msgid "Verify after every setup change"
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:27
msgid "Before consent, check that no optional tracker requests are made."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:28
msgid ""
"After consent, confirm script and event requests use the expected host/path, "
"and check the vendor dashboard for the real test event."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/proxy-guides.php:29
msgid ""
"Withdraw consent and confirm processing stops. Check Proxy diagnostics for "
"recent transport results; unknown or stale endpoints still need verification."
msgstr ""

